WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.857
Good variable names make code easier to understand.

00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:13.442
Monthly_sales is descriptive, and patient_age is clear because the words are separated with an underscore.

00:00:13.442 --> 00:00:21.845
Short names such as ms might save a few keystrokes, but they force the reader to guess what the variable means.

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:24.689
There are also syntax rules.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:29.919
A variable name cannot begin with a number, and it cannot contain spaces.

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:35.854
Python programmers commonly use lowercase words separated by underscores.

00:00:35.854 --> 00:00:41.109
A useful test is to imagine opening your code again six months from now.

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:46.775
If the names still make sense without extra explanation, they are probably good names.
